{
  "requirement": "Marks an agent request that can still accept reusable context before adding node contents.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub struct ContextPhase;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.ContextPhase` is an API-declaration requirement. It says `ContextPhase` marks a request that can still accept context, and it gives the declaration `pub struct ContextPhase;`. The only testable obligation is that the SDK exports a public unit struct `ContextPhase` matching that declaration.\n\nThe requirement's `:test:` anchor and a `{test}` reference both point to `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]`. That test:\n- Runs `cargo doc` for the crate and walks every exported item in the rustdoc HTML (`documented_exports`).\n- Looks up the declaration requirement for each non-module export, and fails if one is missing.\n- Calls `check_declaration` for each export. It extracts the `rust,ignore` block from the requirement text and checks the description is non-empty.\n- Compares the requirement's trait-impl and member sets with rustdoc's. For `ContextPhase` the expected sets are empty.\n- Compares the normalized declaration from the requirement with rustdoc's published declaration, using `signature_parts` on both sides and asserting no differences either way. A changed or missing `pub struct ContextPhase;` (a non-unit struct, a different kind, or a different name) therefore fails the test.\n- Asserts that the set of exports and their kinds equals the inventory, so removing or renaming `ContextPhase` also fails.\n\nThe role the text describes is that `ask` starts in `ContextPhase` and only that phase exposes `context`. That behavior is carried by the separate requirements `judge.phases` and `agent_context`, and by `ValidationContext.ask`. The subject's own text adds no further conditional behavior, so I found no unmapped obligation or gap. There are no acknowledgments.",
  "references": "34070f30c190da855a0af0db8758db88cea74ad388475c8cd2f1dfaa1fb9eb00",
